Z||000010||Formula88||07-09-2001||10:42 PM||||A few things can cause a random reboot.  Dirty power and overheating.  Make sure your PC isn't getting too hot.  Check to see that the fans haven't gotten full of dust, etc.  Your power supply or surge protector could be on the way out.  Also check to make sure all the power cables are plugged in tight.  If you have health monitoring software, check to see what temperature your mobo and CPU are running at.  Intel specs 80*C as the max operating temp of a Pentium III CuMine.  That will, of course vary depending on your processor.  Point of reference, my Pentium III 600e has been running at 800Mhz for over a year now, and running Setiathome continuously, it rarely gets over 60*C.||||reg||6
